Patient "1": a-CGH showed microduplication in 7p22.2 region spanning 371.165 kb (positions 3074785 to 3445950) and microduplication in 12q13.3 region spanning 345.669 kb (positions 56670637 to 57016306). Real-time PCR confirmed both CNVs. Both CNVs classified as variants of uncertain significance (VUS) per ACMG. Cognitive development NVIQ = 93. No congenital malformations. Facial dysmorphism noted. No further chromosomal analyses or segregation analysis performed.\n\nPatient "2": a-CGH showed microduplication of 455.143 kb from position 2967525 to 3422668 in 7p22.2 region inherited from unaffected father. Real-time PCR confirmed CNV. Classified as VUS per ACMG. Clinical evaluation at 36 months revealed expressive language impairment, motor coordination deficit, flat foot, knee valgus, mild dysmorphic traits (slightly upslanting palpebral fissures, low-set protruding ears with prominent lobes, hypoplastic alae nasi with depressed nasal tip). No congenital malformations. Audiological exam normal hearing, scared by loud noises. Attention deficit noted. No hearing loss detected.'
